From: hmbs <hmbs@local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Honour Conan-provided GTest targets

(a) Upstream guards the test link with if(GTEST_FOUND) (all caps).
That spelling is only defined by CMake's bundled FindGTest.cmake
(MODULE mode). This package resolves GTest through CMakeDeps in CONFIG
mode, which only defines GTest_FOUND, so the condition is always false
and configure falls into FetchContent cloning googletest from GitHub,
which fails on the offline CI worker. Accept GTest_FOUND, GTEST_FOUND,
or the existence of the GTest::gtest target.

(b) The true branch links GTest::GTest / GTest::Main, the legacy MODULE
mode aliases. Conan gtest/1.17.0.1 only declares GTest::gtest,
GTest::gtest_main, GTest::gmock and GTest::gmock_main. Link GTest::gtest
only (test/testMain.cpp ships its own main(), so gtest_main is not
wanted).

Mirrors archives/m/memtailor/1.4 patch 0002 (same upstream flaw).

--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -94,17 +94,17 @@
     test/testMain.cpp
     )
 
   ################################
   # add gtest testing ############
   ################################
-  if(NOT GTEST_FOUND)
+  if(NOT GTest_FOUND AND NOT GTEST_FOUND AND NOT TARGET GTest::gtest)
     find_package(GTest)
   endif()
   include(GoogleTest)
   gtest_discover_tests(mathicgb-unit-tests TEST_PREFIX unit-tests:)
 
-  if(GTEST_FOUND)
-    target_link_libraries(mathicgb-unit-tests mathicgb GTest::GTest GTest::Main)
+  if(GTest_FOUND OR GTEST_FOUND OR TARGET GTest::gtest)
+    target_link_libraries(mathicgb-unit-tests mathicgb GTest::gtest)
   else()
     include(FetchContent)
     FetchContent_Declare(googletest
